mode: "100644"
text: "# LinkedIn company pages 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (LinkedIn ships algorithm + product changes often).*\n\n## The POV: the page is a credibility hub + paid launchpad, not the reach engine\nLinkedIn **structurally rebalanced** the feed: **company pages get ~1–5% of feed allocation** (personal\nprofiles ~65%), and **company-page organic reach fell 60–66% (2024→2026)** — page posts reach only **~1.6–5%\nof followers.** **Personal profiles outperform pages by ~5–8× engagement** (headline GaggleAMP figures cite\n~561% reach / 5×; the conservative independent benchmark — **Sprout Q1 2026 — is ~4.7% personal vs ~1–2%\ncompany**, directionally the same). **People connect with people, not logos:** the algorithm **trusts\nindividuals over brands** (personal = authentic voice; company = marketing agenda); **trust in personal\ncontent is ~3× higher**; **92% of B2B buyers trust employee recommendations over advertising.**\n\n## What the page is irreplaceably FOR\n**Credibility/legitimacy** (buyers check it), the **official record** (announcements), **recruitment/career\npages**, the **Follow button + website plugin**, **product pages**, **Page analytics** — and critically the\n**paid launchpad:** **LinkedIn Ads run exclusively from company pages**, and **Thought Leader Ads** (promote\na *personal* profile's post with paid targeting) require the page. **Content assignment:** announcements /\njobs / paid assets → **page**; thought leadership / opinions / stories → **personal**; product & case studies\n→ **both.**\n\n## Employee advocacy = the primary organic lever\n- **Employees collectively have ~10× the company's connections.** **Only ~3% of employees share, yet drive\n  ~30% of company engagement.** Employee posts get **~2.75× impressions / ~5× engagement** vs the page\n  (despite ~46% fewer followers); **employee-sourced leads convert ~7×**, and activating employee networks\n  yields **~5× more leads** than the page alone. **CEO/exec content ~4×** an average page post.\n- **First-hour signal:** employees engaging with a page post **within ~60 min** reads as a strong quality\n  signal and **extends reach.**\n- **Run the program right:** leadership buy-in via the math (20 employees × 500 connections = 10,000 reach vs\n  5,000 followers); **frictionless** (provide shareable content + suggested commentary employees\n  **personalize** — a personal opener/opinion/question dramatically lifts performance; **never identical\n  copy**); **pilot** of natural advocates; light **gamification**; LinkedIn's **Notify Employees** for\n  high-priority posts. The employees post **from their own profiles** (→ `linkedin-growth`).\n\n## Page content that still works organically\n- **Carousel/document posts** (top **saves** — saves ~5× a like) and **short vertical video (<90s) with\n  captions** (+80% reach); **custom images get 2× more comments.** **Text-only is dead on pages (~0.42×\n  reach).** **External links in the body cut reach ~60% → put links in comments.** **Questions / structured\n  frameworks** that spark multi-threaded discussion get **437% more views.** **Depth Score (2026):** dwell\n  time, comment depth, saves, private shares — not clicks. **Engagement-bait suppressed; pods → shadowban;\n  hashtags minimal (3–5).**\n\n## Cadence, growth + native features\n- **Consistency (weekly+) → ~5.6× more followers**; respond to comments fast; the **first 60 min** matters; a\n  **150-follower threshold** accelerates growth ~9×. **Native features:** Notify Employees, Showcase Pages,\n  Events, Newsletters, Products, the Follow plugin, Page analytics, Thought Leader Ads, and **Creator\n  Marketplace / BrandWorks** (B2B creator discovery, launched June 2026). **Track:** followers, reach,\n  engagement, and **advocacy reach + UTM-tracked conversions** (prove ROI).\n"
